# A pair as a declared data family of one constructor and two fields. plover_pair is the
# prelude's pair under the marker $constructor, the identity, so that binding it as the
# family's constructor leaves the prelude's pair an ordinary term, as native_types/list
# does for cons. plover_pair_type first second is the pairs whose fields are in first and
# in second; it is a term of its own, not the constructor, since a family's identity is
# its criterion.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "native_types") "markers")
λ _ $constructor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. $constructor λl r p. p l r)
λ plover_pair
. (λtuple. tuple λ first second. plover_pair first second)
λ plover_pair_type
. export plover_pair plover_pair_type
